# Implementation Plan: ProteinScope Bioinformatics Pipeline

A full-stack, automated end-to-end protein bioinformatics and missense variant pathogenicity analysis system (**ProteinScope**). It accepts a UniProt accession code (e.g., `P04637`, `P0DTC2`) and optional missense mutation (e.g., `R175H`), executing multi-pathway data ingestion, sequence analysis, BLAST homology, 3D structure retrieval & validation, PyMOL scripting, interactive WebGL 3D dashboard generation, evolutionary & PPI comparative analysis, unsupervised ML feature clustering, NGS variant mapping, ClinVar supervised pathogenicity classification, multi-protein benchmarking, and multi-format report generation.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Environment & Dependency Architecture**:
> - Biopython, pandas, numpy, scikit-learn, matplotlib, scipy, PyYAML, python-docx, and fpdf are configured in the virtual environment (`bioinfo_env`).
> - **Dual Operational Modes**: Full Online Mode (queries UniProt, NCBI QBLAST, RCSB PDB, AlphaFold DB, SWISS-MODEL, InterPro, and STRING DB) and Full Offline Mode (reuses cached JSON/XML/PDB fixtures and local ClinVar models).
> - **3D Visualization & Web Dashboard**: Produces standard PyMOL `.pml`/`.pse` scripts, high-resolution Matplotlib 3D figures, and a standalone, zero-dependency interactive WebGL dashboard (`protein_viewer.html`) powered by `3Dmol.js`.
> - **Variant Pathogenicity ML**: Integrates ClinVar-trained Random Forest models with 15+ structural, physicochemical, and evolutionary features to predict mutation impact with SHAP-like biological justifications.

