## CLI Usage & Hosting Guide

### CLI Commands

```powershell
# Standard sequence & structure analysis
.\bioinfo_env\Scripts\python.exe main.py P0DTC2

# Pathogenicity prediction for specific missense mutation (auto-trains classifier if needed)
.\bioinfo_env\Scripts\python.exe main.py P04637 --mutation R175H

# Offline mode with cached data
.\bioinfo_env\Scripts\python.exe main.py P04637 --mutation R175H --offline-blast --offline

# Run full multi-protein benchmark suite
.\bioinfo_env\Scripts\python.exe benchmark.py

# Run unit tests
.\bioinfo_env\Scripts\python.exe -m unittest discover tests
```

### Hosting & Viewing the Interactive Website

The pipeline outputs an interactive 3D WebGL dashboard to `output/<ACCESSION>/report/protein_viewer.html`.

1. **Local HTTP Server (Recommended)**:
   ```powershell
   .\bioinfo_env\Scripts\python.exe -m http.server 8080 --directory output
   ```
   Open in browser: `http://localhost:8080/P04637/report/protein_viewer.html` or `http://localhost:8080/P0DTC2/report/protein_viewer.html`

2. **Direct Browser Launch**:
   ```powershell
   Start-Process "output\P04637\report\protein_viewer.html"
   ```

3. **Public Deployment**:
   - Drag & drop the `output/` directory directly onto [Netlify Drop](https://app.netlify.com/drop) or [Vercel](https://vercel.com).
   - Or commit the `output/` folder into a GitHub repository and enable **GitHub Pages** in repository settings.

